{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-smooth","title":"prop:volume-form-smooth","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1410,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:volume-form-smooth","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-determinant]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:volume-form-smooth","line":2393,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Riemannian Volume Form is Smooth]\n\\label{prop:volume-form-smooth}\n\n\\uses{def:volume-form-pointwise, def:smooth-orientation, prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames, lem:top-forms-proportional, prop:volume-form-determinant, prop:volume-form-value-one, lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth}\n\n\n\n\nFor a Riemannian $n$-manifold with smooth orientation, the family $dV_g$ is a smooth $n$-form.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames,lem:top-forms-proportional,prop:volume-form-determinant,prop:volume-form-value-one,lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth}\n\\sketch In a tangent-bundle trivialization, read $dV_g|_x$ as an $n$-form $\\Phi(x)$ on $\\mathbb R^n$. Fix a basis $b$ and a local oriented orthonormal frame $Z_i$. Since $\\Phi(x_0)\\ne0$, its value on the basis $b$ is nonzero. Lemma \\ref{lem:top-forms-proportional} expresses $\\Phi(x)$ as a scalar multiple of $\\Phi(x_0)$, with scalar $\\Phi(x)(b)/\\Phi(x_0)(b)$. Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-determinant} writes the numerator as the determinant of the smooth pairings $\\langle Z_i,e^{-1}b_j\\rangle_g$, hence the scalar and $\\Phi$ are smooth.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Riemannian Volume Form is Smooth] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a766f6c756d652d666f726d2d736d6f6f7468\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Avolume-form-pointwise\">↗ def:volume-form-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\">↗ def:smooth-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aoriented-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-forms-proportional\">↗ lem:top-forms-proportional</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-determinant\">↗ prop:volume-form-determinant</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainner-product-vector-fields-smooth\">↗ lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth</a> <p></p>For a Riemannian <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold with smooth orientation, the family <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g$\">$dV_g$</span> is a smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-form.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aoriented-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-forms-proportional\">↗ lem:top-forms-proportional</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-determinant\">↗ prop:volume-form-determinant</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainner-product-vector-fields-smooth\">↗ lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth</a> \\sketch In a tangent-bundle trivialization, read <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g|_x$\">$dV_g|_x$</span> as an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-form <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (x)$\">$\\Phi (x)$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb R^n$\">$\\mathbb R^n$</span>. Fix a basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b$\">$b$</span> and a local oriented orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Z_i$\">$Z_i$</span>. Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (x_0)\\ne 0$\">$\\Phi (x_0)\\ne 0$</span>, its value on the basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b$\">$b$</span> is nonzero. Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-forms-proportional\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a746f702d666f726d732d70726f706f7274696f6e616c\">12</a> expresses <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (x)$\">$\\Phi (x)$</span> as a scalar multiple of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (x_0)$\">$\\Phi (x_0)$</span>, with scalar <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (x)(b)/\\Phi (x_0)(b)$\">$\\Phi (x)(b)/\\Phi (x_0)(b)$</span>. Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-determinant\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-determinant\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a766f6c756d652d666f726d2d64657465726d696e616e74\">12</a> writes the numerator as the determinant of the smooth pairings <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle Z_i,e^{-1}b_j\\rangle _g$\">$\\langle Z_i,e^{-1}b_j\\rangle _g$</span>, hence the scalar and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi $\">$\\Phi $</span> are smooth. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-coframe","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","label":"def:volume-form-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","label":"def:smooth-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","label":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional","title":"lem:top-forms-proportional","label":"lem:top-forms-proportional"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-determinant","title":"prop:volume-form-determinant","label":"prop:volume-form-determinant"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","label":"prop:volume-form-value-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth","title":"lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth","label":"lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-volume-form","title":"prop:riemannian-volume-form","label":"prop:riemannian-volume-form"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-smooth","title":"prop:volume-form-smooth","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Riemannian Volume Form is Smooth]\n\\label{prop:volume-form-smooth}\n\n\\uses{def:volume-form-pointwise, def:smooth-orientation, prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames, lem:top-forms-proportional, prop:volume-form-determinant, prop:volume-form-value-one, lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth}\n\n\n\n\nFor a Riemannian $n$-manifold with smooth orientation, the family $dV_g$ is a smooth $n$-form.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames,lem:top-forms-proportional,prop:volume-form-determinant,prop:volume-form-value-one,lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth}\n\\sketch In a tangent-bundle trivialization, read $dV_g|_x$ as an $n$-form $\\Phi(x)$ on $\\mathbb R^n$. Fix a basis $b$ and a local oriented orthonormal frame $Z_i$. Since $\\Phi(x_0)\\ne0$, its value on the basis $b$ is nonzero. Lemma \\ref{lem:top-forms-proportional} expresses $\\Phi(x)$ as a scalar multiple of $\\Phi(x_0)$, with scalar $\\Phi(x)(b)/\\Phi(x_0)(b)$. Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-determinant} writes the numerator as the determinant of the smooth pairings $\\langle Z_i,e^{-1}b_j\\rangle_g$, hence the scalar and $\\Phi$ are smooth.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional","title":"lem:top-forms-proportional","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-determinant","title":"prop:volume-form-determinant","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth","title":"lem:inner-product-vector-fields-smooth","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}